| Description | An SOP of N steps whose initialisation yields N nonces bound to that instance (`x_i = H^i(s)`, anchor `x_N` public). Step k presents `x_(N-(k+1))`; accepted iff it hashes to the last accepted element. Cannot skip, cannot reorder, nonces invalid outside the instance; credit at each step requires the nonce and the performance criterion (`r_k = H(x_step ‖ result_k)`). Companion term for a fixed procedure over random contents: parametricity. |
| Steps | init (seed, anchor) → step k: present `x_(N-(k+1))` + criterion → verify `H(x) == last_accepted` → receipt → … → close (receipt `H(x_0 ‖ head)`) |
